WEBVTT

00:04.630 --> 00:05.880
We're a pair!

00:06.140 --> 00:07.890
Right! A pair forever!

00:08.430 --> 00:15.600
Cut your finger and promise. Break it
and you'll have to swallow a thousand needles!

00:35.380 --> 00:44.150
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

00:44.190 --> 00:53.190
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

00:53.230 --> 00:59.960
Constantly searching,
still can't find

01:02.570 --> 01:08.640
Ever illusive peace of mind

01:10.810 --> 01:19.380
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

01:19.420 --> 01:26.020
And I'm faced with another day

01:27.230 --> 01:32.960
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:33.000 --> 01:37.300
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

01:37.340 --> 01:41.780
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:41.810 --> 01:46.210
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

01:46.250 --> 01:50.740
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:50.790 --> 01:58.630
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

02:04.640 --> 02:07.970
Hinoenma

02:08.130 --> 02:11.960
I'm searching for a woman;
a pitiful woman who is precious to me.

02:12.720 --> 02:14.390
My father is going crazy.

02:14.640 --> 02:15.640
She's a demon;

02:15.850 --> 02:16.980
a Hinoenma!

02:20.730 --> 02:22.820
(Note: Maen are demons that obstruct Buddhist scholarship and training.]

02:20.830 --> 02:22.610
"A Maen that flies towards us".

02:22.710 --> 02:25.040
Based on the legend that the Maen
Maara appeared in the form of a woman

02:25.040 --> 02:27.890
when it attempted to hinder
Buddha's attainment of Nirvana,

02:27.710 --> 02:30.740
the term came to represent
youkai who acted like evil women.

02:30.820 --> 02:33.410
It is said that Maen will take
the form of a beautiful woman,

02:33.440 --> 02:37.020
and drain their male victims of their
life energy every night until they perish.

02:43.030 --> 02:44.990
Exterminate the Hinoenma?

02:45.770 --> 02:48.070
In other words, is it something like this?:

02:48.780 --> 02:54.070
[Note: Kaisendonya were businesses that mediated contracts
between shipping merchants and their clientele.]

02:48.780 --> 02:50.940
The master of a kaisendonya, Kyouemon,

02:51.070 --> 02:54.070
is searching for his bride, who ran
away on the night of their wedding.

02:54.240 --> 02:54.860
Yes.

02:56.990 --> 02:59.200
The woman suffered from a
pyromania-induced penchant to commit arson,

02:59.450 --> 03:02.080
and ran away from him
because she was troubled by her illness.

03:02.450 --> 03:04.830
And now that he has built
another house that she can set fire to,

03:04.960 --> 03:06.830
he says she can come back without fear.

03:07.210 --> 03:08.460
On the contrary...

03:08.920 --> 03:14.420
If it's something she can't stop doing, then I'll let her
burn as much as she wants without bothering anyone.

03:14.630 --> 03:18.630
If it can be cured, good... but if
nothing works, then I'm willing to die with her.

03:19.800 --> 03:24.220
Then... why don't we hand her
over and let him fulfill his desire?

03:24.850 --> 03:27.260
H-Hey, wait!

03:27.350 --> 03:29.850
Do you know where this Shiragiku-san,
or whatever her name may be, is right now?

03:29.890 --> 03:30.970
We do.

03:31.310 --> 03:33.430
Wh-What do you mean?

03:34.140 --> 03:35.730
Evil knows its own kind.

03:36.440 --> 03:37.230
That's right.

03:37.610 --> 03:39.480
We'll first need to meet the priest Ryoujun.

03:39.650 --> 03:45.440
That "wordly" pries... He's probably off wandering,
through the red light districts around the border of town.

03:45.900 --> 03:49.740
Well, in terms of worldliness,
he'd probably lose to Shiragiku.

03:50.030 --> 03:51.660
You know her?

03:52.070 --> 03:52.870
Sort of...

03:55.200 --> 03:58.620
She deals in underground businesses, just like us.

03:59.120 --> 04:03.080
But she's not easy to deal with. She's pretty ill-tempered.

04:03.380 --> 04:04.670
Y-You know her that much?!

04:05.170 --> 04:07.670
She's so nasty that even Ogin would run
away from her naked, just so she could run faster--

04:07.670 --> 04:08.790
What'd you say?

04:09.250 --> 04:10.670
Then I have to tell him!

04:11.760 --> 04:13.630
I'm going to go and talk to Kyouemon-san!

04:14.050 --> 04:14.840
Wait!

04:15.470 --> 04:16.300
Why?

04:17.470 --> 04:20.550
Don't you think you're
misunderstanding something, sensei?

04:21.140 --> 04:22.890
Our job isn't to help people.

04:23.180 --> 04:26.810
We deceive people, and even kill them once in a while.

04:27.100 --> 04:28.600
We dredge gutters in the human psyche.

04:29.060 --> 04:33.690
We can die at any time, and that's
just the way things are in this business.

04:34.320 --> 04:38.070
Yuck. If you're going to die, die alone, Komatakuguri.

04:38.110 --> 04:40.360
[Note: Yamanekomawashi means puppeteer.]

04:38.110 --> 04:40.360
Cut the jokes, Yamanekomawashi.

04:40.450 --> 04:41.950
I'd thought better of you guys!

04:44.280 --> 04:47.450
Oh well... Anyway, this does the trick.

04:47.740 --> 04:49.160
We'll miss him.

04:49.620 --> 04:50.620
YOU'LL miss him!

04:51.230 --> 04:52.910
Don't talk nonsense!

04:53.580 --> 04:54.370
More importantly...

04:54.830 --> 04:58.040
How troublesome... It's Shiragiku.

05:04.800 --> 05:05.750
All right!

05:08.130 --> 05:13.050
If that's how it is, then I'll just have to
find Shiragiku-san before Mataichi-san's group!

05:14.100 --> 05:15.720
Don't worry.

05:16.350 --> 05:17.890
I'll return right away to Kitabayashi.

05:18.560 --> 05:20.890
I'm just going to settle
something that happened in the past.

05:30.190 --> 05:30.820
All right!

05:34.030 --> 05:34.570
Sir!

05:40.700 --> 05:41.700
Thanks.

05:47.660 --> 05:49.580
What a beautiful lady...

06:04.800 --> 06:06.680
I'm not really comfortable in a place like this.

06:09.050 --> 06:10.180
He came.

06:10.310 --> 06:12.390
Mister, you're a hunk.

06:12.890 --> 06:16.520
Come, come. Gome in. If you're
not sure, both of us can take care of you.

06:16.680 --> 06:18.480
No, I'd rather not!

06:20.810 --> 06:23.020
The hell do you think you're doing?

06:23.060 --> 06:24.060
Excuse me.

06:24.070 --> 06:25.230
You from Edo?

06:25.360 --> 06:27.650
If you think you're better than
rest of us, you'll lose your nuts, man!

06:27.780 --> 06:29.940
What're you wrangling with him for?

06:30.070 --> 06:32.990
What, a priest?

06:33.110 --> 06:34.570
What are you doing in a place like this?

06:34.620 --> 06:37.490
You fools! You don't know me,
a man who is feared in Inabashi?!

06:39.160 --> 06:40.240
Hey, a hot girl!

06:41.330 --> 06:41.660
This way!

06:44.000 --> 06:45.460
Stop!!!

06:46.210 --> 06:47.120
What's going on?

06:50.670 --> 06:52.000
Where did they go?

06:52.050 --> 06:53.130
Wait up!

06:55.260 --> 06:56.760
Thank you.

06:57.220 --> 06:59.340
You need to be on your toes around here,

06:59.380 --> 07:03.180
but you don't seem like the type of
person who would come here, anyway.

07:03.550 --> 07:05.220
What are you doing in a place like this?

07:06.430 --> 07:09.560
I came to look for a monk named Ryoujun-sama.

07:09.730 --> 07:12.180
Oh? That would be me.

07:12.350 --> 07:14.020
What? You're him?

07:14.060 --> 07:16.020
Yup. What do you want?

07:16.060 --> 07:19.230
I need some information on a girl named Shiragiku...

07:19.360 --> 07:20.610
Shiragiku?!

07:21.480 --> 07:22.690
Let's talk somewhere else.

07:31.870 --> 07:32.570
Two of them?

07:32.780 --> 07:34.200
I can't stand this rain.

07:38.370 --> 07:40.500
Oh, someone got here ahead of us?

07:40.790 --> 07:43.460
Eh, I don't mind. It's raining pretty nasty, after all.

07:47.300 --> 07:49.630
Don't stay in the corner like that,
come warm yourself by the fire.

07:50.960 --> 07:53.260
Well, we've got a young man here, after all.

07:53.680 --> 07:55.260
So, we were talking about Tatsuta, weren't we?

07:55.760 --> 07:58.510
Oh, no. What I wanted to ask was...

07:58.550 --> 08:01.680
Ah, right. It was about Shiragiku, right? Shiragiku.

08:02.140 --> 08:05.350
Well, even though I know who you're talking about,
I can't help but mention the other name, too.

08:05.350 --> 08:07.180
It's like they're a pair.

08:07.190 --> 08:07.980
A pair?

08:08.730 --> 08:11.230
It happened a long time ago.

08:11.730 --> 08:15.860
She was a beauty, pretty as a flower.

08:18.280 --> 08:20.320
Back then, if you were the daughter of a merchant,

08:20.320 --> 08:24.030
you'd be learning how to dance and play musical
instruments from the time when you were a little kid.

08:24.030 --> 08:27.530
Oh, Shiragiku was said to be
the daughter of some nobleman.

08:27.830 --> 08:29.870
She was reserved and graceful;

08:30.040 --> 08:33.620
not the type to go ahead and try things on her own,

08:33.750 --> 08:36.870
but she excelled at anything she did.

08:37.540 --> 08:42.380
Shiragiku was always with her good friend,
Tatsuta, who was the daughter of a lumber merchant.

08:43.130 --> 08:46.630
This Tatsuta was a real nice girl, too.

08:47.220 --> 08:50.720
She always held Shiragiku's hand.

08:51.840 --> 08:54.680
If you're going, Tatsuta-chan, I'll go, too!

08:54.970 --> 08:56.640
We'll always be together!

08:56.680 --> 08:58.390
Yup! We'll be a pair forever!

08:58.430 --> 09:00.270
A pair forever!

09:00.560 --> 09:01.560
A "pair".

09:01.640 --> 09:04.850
So they said, but Shiragiku was always number one.

09:05.150 --> 09:06.600
She was that kind of girl.

09:07.820 --> 09:12.820
[Note: Yukata is a casual type of kimono worn in the summertime.]

09:07.820 --> 09:11.820
I forgot when exactly, but one day,
when they were wearing the same yukata...

09:13.360 --> 09:14.490
We'll be a pair!

09:14.610 --> 09:16.530
Right! A pair forever!

09:17.740 --> 09:19.860
That's a really beautiful yukata.

09:20.070 --> 09:22.530
It really suits you, Shiragiku-chan!

09:23.830 --> 09:29.210
It was a sad thing for Tatsuta...
Shiragiku being the only one who was praised.

09:29.500 --> 09:34.500
Oh, I was intending to talk about Shiragiku,
but I ended up talking about Tatsuta.

09:34.840 --> 09:36.790
It's because the two were always together, you see.

09:37.460 --> 09:41.550
The sun shined all the more brightly on Shiragiku-chan.

09:41.630 --> 09:43.840
That was how it felt.

09:44.130 --> 09:45.180
Light?

09:45.470 --> 09:50.760
When she was abojat 14,
Shiragiku went to serve the feudal lord of Saigoku.

09:51.010 --> 09:52.310
It'll be fine!

09:52.600 --> 09:53.930
I'll write to you.

09:54.390 --> 09:56.520
Even if we're apart, it'll be fine!

09:56.890 --> 09:59.060
We're a pair forever, right?

09:59.150 --> 10:00.190
Yup! A pair!

10:00.520 --> 10:02.860
But she soon returned.

10:03.480 --> 10:04.190
Why?

10:04.610 --> 10:09.030
There was a case of a suspected arson in the inner section
of the feudal lord's house, and it was blamed on Shiragiku...

10:09.400 --> 10:13.490
but it was probably because the
women there were jealous of her beauty.

10:14.910 --> 10:17.490
I was able to meet you again, Tatsuta-chan!

10:17.870 --> 10:19.910
That's enough for me.

10:23.790 --> 10:26.670
Then, there was another fire.

10:29.960 --> 10:31.040
Are you okay?

10:32.130 --> 10:33.000
That surprised me.

10:33.380 --> 10:35.760
This time it was Shiragiku's house that burned.

10:36.010 --> 10:37.800
Her parents died in that fire,

10:38.010 --> 10:39.800
and it was another suspicious fire to boot, right?

10:40.340 --> 10:43.350
A rumor that Shiragiku attracts
fire spread throughout the town.

10:43.430 --> 10:47.470
Shiragiku was eventually chased out of
the city and was forced to turn to prostitution.

10:47.970 --> 10:52.980
But even then, the sun still shone upon her.

10:53.310 --> 10:56.690
In just a short time, she became a
famous prostitute with many admirers.

10:57.440 --> 10:59.900
The light always shone on her.

11:08.780 --> 11:11.070
Oh, did she leave?

11:11.660 --> 11:13.240
The rain must have stopped.

11:14.200 --> 11:17.620
Before long, a man willing to free
Shiragiku from prostitution appeared.

11:17.830 --> 11:20.080
He was a lumber merchant named Seihachi.

11:20.460 --> 11:23.920
At last, I thought she would be able to achieve happiness,

11:24.170 --> 11:27.380
but just as they were about to marry,
Seihachi was offered an arranged marriage.

11:27.550 --> 11:29.960
Tatsuta was the one whom Seihachi was offered.

11:31.220 --> 11:33.470
Well, since their families were both lumber merchants,

11:33.680 --> 11:38.350
his family must have convinced him
that Tatsuta would make the better bride.

11:38.800 --> 11:42.770
Shiragiku chopped off her
little finger and sent it to Seihachi.

11:43.220 --> 11:44.140
Her finger?

11:44.560 --> 11:45.350
Indeed.

11:45.640 --> 11:48.390
"Finger cutting" isn't just a children's game.

11:48.770 --> 11:54.520
It is also a sorrowful custom among
prostitutes to express your feelings to your lover.

11:55.280 --> 12:00.280
Well, it wasn't certain which of the
two he loved, and it never will be now.

12:00.530 --> 12:01.400
By which, you mean...?

12:01.700 --> 12:04.570
He died on the night of his wedding.

12:05.200 --> 12:05.820
It couldn't have been...

12:05.870 --> 12:06.990
Yes, a fire.

12:07.580 --> 12:09.370
At the height of the wedding celebration, too.

12:09.490 --> 12:12.200
A huge fire that spread all the way to the city of Oosaka.

12:12.830 --> 12:17.790
Seihachi, and his bride, Tatsuta, were both burnt to ashes.

12:20.250 --> 12:21.880
Then, Shiragiku-san...

12:22.050 --> 12:24.210
Who knows? But you know...

12:24.420 --> 12:27.090
to have the man you love taken
from you by your childhood friend...

12:27.380 --> 12:29.680
She was consumed by the flames of hatred and envy.

12:29.760 --> 12:32.090
It's better to think of it that way.

12:32.430 --> 12:38.520
It would have been too sad for her to celebrate the
wedding between the man she loved and her best friend.

12:38.890 --> 12:39.850
Don't you think so?

12:44.040 --> 12:45.790
What happened after that, I don't know.

12:46.040 --> 12:50.170
She returned to being a prostitute,
and was involved in some rather shady dealings.

12:50.840 --> 12:54.630
Perhaps she really was a Hinoenma.

12:54.800 --> 12:56.760
And where is Shiragiku-san now?

12:56.840 --> 12:58.300
Wasn't she in Nagoya?

12:59.470 --> 13:02.220
I got an announcement about her upcoming wedding...

13:03.980 --> 13:07.350
I'm going back to Nagoya.
What about you, Ryoujun-san?

13:07.390 --> 13:09.190
I'll pass.

13:09.230 --> 13:14.520
Even if she did send an invitation,
I suppose she'd rather I didn't come.

13:25.870 --> 13:26.780
Ryoujun-san?

13:26.830 --> 13:30.040
In the end, I decided to come.

13:36.630 --> 13:39.540
Something's... bothering me.

13:40.500 --> 13:41.290
What is it?

13:44.210 --> 13:45.130
Her little finger!

13:45.670 --> 13:47.220
Shifagiku-san should be missing her little finger!

13:52.890 --> 13:55.760
That Tatsuta was a real nice girl, too.

13:59.980 --> 14:04.810
My beloved darling, I have
prepared for our wedding and am waiting.

14:06.310 --> 14:09.520
Are you saying you love me...? That you love Shiragiku?

14:12.650 --> 14:17.530
He shouldn't have come... He knows Shiragiku's past!

14:22.030 --> 14:24.240
Do you suppose Shiragiku is coming?

14:24.860 --> 14:27.960
That depends on how much you believe.

14:29.210 --> 14:32.920
He's going to let her set fire
to that? Isn't that a big luxury?

14:33.040 --> 14:35.380
To each his own, that's what.

14:36.210 --> 14:38.420
It'll be over as soon as the sensei gets here.

14:45.430 --> 14:46.840
F-Fire?!

14:47.100 --> 14:48.970
Wait, Ryoujun-san!

14:49.260 --> 14:53.220
Huh? That's so mean of him to
run away without even waking me!

14:57.390 --> 14:59.600
Ryoujun-san! Ryoujun-san!!!

15:05.610 --> 15:07.190
T-That's...

15:09.200 --> 15:11.530
Why is she here?

15:12.240 --> 15:16.370
Why is she laughing when she
watches us... when she watches the fire?

15:16.910 --> 15:17.740
She can't be...

15:18.080 --> 15:19.620
Is she Shiragiku?

15:30.670 --> 15:33.050
Sensei, wait a second!

15:36.220 --> 15:37.300
HAGS!

15:38.840 --> 15:41.260
We can't let you interfere.

15:41.510 --> 15:42.640
We won't let you.

15:47.430 --> 15:50.430
If Shiragiku-san gets to the Kaneshiro house before me...

15:53.150 --> 15:54.980
I believe in you, Mataichi-san.

15:55.690 --> 15:57.770
You'll save Kyouemon-san, right?

15:58.480 --> 16:01.110
If he tries to die, you won't leave him, will you?

16:09.410 --> 16:11.450
I've been waiting fon you, Shiragiku!

16:11.530 --> 16:13.740
Come! Burn as much as you like!

16:17.210 --> 16:18.080
What's wrong?

16:18.540 --> 16:19.540
Come here.

16:20.080 --> 16:27.750
I can't. I, Shiragiku, sent my finger to my beloved!

16:29.090 --> 16:30.590
The bride is here!

16:37.680 --> 16:38.640
Her little finger...?!

16:43.020 --> 16:43.850
Wait!

16:44.140 --> 16:45.390
Hey, wait!

16:46.020 --> 16:48.310
She's not Shiragiku-san!

16:48.770 --> 16:53.230
It's all right, Shiragiku. It doesn't matter whom you love.

16:53.270 --> 16:55.860
Come. Burn to your heart's content.

17:01.030 --> 17:03.030
Shiragiku!

17:04.370 --> 17:05.490
Kyouemon-sama!

17:05.780 --> 17:10.540
Oh, Shiragiku... how I've
waited for you; how I've longed for you!

17:10.950 --> 17:13.460
Those eyes, that hair...

17:13.580 --> 17:16.080
I never forgot them, even for a day.

17:17.130 --> 17:18.580
Kyouemon-sama!

17:19.540 --> 17:22.000
I'm the real one. That's right, isn't it?

17:22.710 --> 17:24.300
Shiragiku!

17:28.840 --> 17:30.470
Shiragiku!

17:30.590 --> 17:32.800
You should be dead! I killed you!

17:33.050 --> 17:35.220
Killed me... yes.

17:35.640 --> 17:37.270
The same thing is happening, isn't it?

17:37.520 --> 17:39.810
No, our situations were reversed.

17:40.730 --> 17:43.810
I came to celebrate your wedding...

17:45.560 --> 17:49.480
I wish for your lifelong happiness.

18:01.990 --> 18:03.490
Why am I the only one who...?

18:03.740 --> 18:04.870
Why am I...?

18:07.660 --> 18:09.710
You won't look at me, either, will you?

18:11.460 --> 18:12.330
At me!

18:17.050 --> 18:19.670
We promised... we're a pair, right?

18:29.180 --> 18:30.310
We're a pair.

18:30.810 --> 18:34.730
And now, we're finally a pair...
you and I, who have never been lit by the light.

18:34.890 --> 18:40.020
Is that why you killed me... and the people I loved?

18:40.270 --> 18:42.560
The sun always shone on you.

18:42.820 --> 18:45.690
As long as you lived, I could gain nothing.

18:45.940 --> 18:47.280
No one would even look at me.

18:47.820 --> 18:49.530
I was always in the shadows.

18:55.870 --> 18:56.700
Mataichi!

18:57.410 --> 18:58.580
Then, you're...

19:01.500 --> 19:03.330
You're a fool.

19:04.330 --> 19:05.370
Kyouemon-san wouldn't have cared,

19:05.580 --> 19:09.540
even if you had been a sinful woman
who commited crimes in Shiragiku's name!

19:10.130 --> 19:11.630
If you had been you...

19:12.050 --> 19:13.340
But all the same, you...

19:14.720 --> 19:15.970
Shiragiku!

19:26.430 --> 19:29.350
His hand... if I take his hand...

19:29.390 --> 19:33.520
I can be happy... The sun will shine down on me!

19:39.730 --> 19:45.070
No... no... he wants her, too!

19:47.240 --> 19:49.490
Shiragiku!!!

19:54.910 --> 19:56.870
The deed is done!

19:58.210 --> 20:00.000
Mataichi-san!

20:02.130 --> 20:04.250
She's not Shiragiku-san!

20:04.670 --> 20:05.500
Sensel?

20:10.510 --> 20:12.890
[Note: Mata no ji is Mataichi's nickname.]

20:10.510 --> 20:12.090
Thanks, Mata no ji.

20:12.720 --> 20:14.130
Thanks to you, I understand...

20:14.840 --> 20:21.350
who truly wants me...
and who it is that I'm truly a pair with.

20:23.060 --> 20:25.350
I... Shiragiku...

20:25.850 --> 20:27.230
will shine while remaining in darkness!

20:39.280 --> 20:43.700
Shiragiku really was a youkai; a Hinoenma.

20:44.490 --> 20:46.910
Kyouemon-sama, your Buddha spirit reached her.

20:47.160 --> 20:52.660
She was a Hinoenma; a fire demon that was
consumed by its own flames and disappeared.

20:53.460 --> 20:55.870
Please, hold a service for her...

20:56.330 --> 20:58.460
for Shiragiku's pitiable soul.

21:00.130 --> 21:03.960
Shiragiku... I didn't care who you were.

21:04.470 --> 21:08.930
No matter if you were Shiragiku, or
a Hinoenma who burnt people to death.

21:11.390 --> 21:13.890
Jeez... you really screwed it up this time.

21:14.140 --> 21:16.390
Well, she had a little finger...

21:16.470 --> 21:21.770
After the fire in Oosaka, Tatsuta took the
place of Shiragiku, whom she admired and hated,

21:21.980 --> 21:24.350
and did evil deeds under Shiragiku's name.

21:25.440 --> 21:28.690
She began setting fires to ruin Shiragiku's reputation,

21:28.860 --> 21:32.610
but over time, she began to set fires for her own pleasure.

21:33.490 --> 21:37.240
That was the perfect chance to defeat Shiragiku.

21:38.830 --> 21:43.240
And after all that work I went
through to keep you out of it, sensei...

21:43.370 --> 21:47.660
Well, I have a pretty good idea as to where she escaped.

21:49.120 --> 21:50.540
But there's a more important problem than that...

21:50.670 --> 21:53.340
Yes, Kyougokutei will...

21:53.790 --> 21:56.550
Things will most likely become very complicated.

21:57.720 --> 21:58.540
Sensei!

22:01.380 --> 22:03.880
It may be time for us to part.

22:05.600 --> 22:09.600
Mataichi-san! Ogin-san! Nagamimi-san!

22:14.480 --> 22:20.570
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:21.920 --> 22:28.010
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:28.990 --> 22:34.760
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:34.800 --> 22:41.430
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:42.800 --> 22:48.740
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:48.780 --> 22:55.440
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:56.280 --> 23:05.750
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:07.060 --> 23:10.260
Draw near

23:10.530 --> 23:17.530
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:17.570 --> 23:23.510
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:25.680 --> 23:30.950
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:30.990 --> 23:39.620
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:48.030 --> 23:53.400
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

23:54.820 --> 23:56.910
A concentrated form of hatred from ancient times;

23:57.320 --> 23:59.910
an accursed cannon technology carved on a person's back.

24:00.280 --> 24:03.080
I must now vanquish my fate.

24:03.370 --> 24:06.080
I will take my deceased son's life.

24:07.200 --> 24:11.240
On the next Kyougoku Natsuhiko's Rumors: 100 Stories,

24:11.830 --> 24:12.910
Funayuurei.

24:13.700 --> 24:16.000
The deed is done.
